# Museum of Twitter - Project Guide

## Overview
A Twitter-like archive system built with SvelteKit and Supabase. Tweets are authored as custom bracket-tag markdown, stored as raw text, and parsed on read (client and server) into structured data for rendering. Admin routes (password-gated) create/edit/import tweets and manage a rotating "featured tweet"; public routes display the archive as a feed and individual permalinked tweets.

This doc describes the codebase as it actually exists, not an aspirational plan — keep it in sync when routes, components, or the schema change.

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend**: SvelteKit 2 (Svelte 5, runes) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4
- **Backend**: Supabase (Postgres + Storage + Auth)
- **Admin auth**: `@supabase/ssr` cookie-based sessions (email+password), session validated server-side in `hooks.server.js` and gated in `admin/+layout.server.js`
- **Custom markdown parser**: hand-written bracket-tag parser (no external markdown library)
- **Font**: self-hosted "TwitterChirp" (`@font-face` rules in `src/app.css`, files in `static/fonts/`)
- **Theming**: CSS variables in `src/app.css`. Public pages default to dark; `data-theme="light"` on `<html>` switches them (set before first paint by an inline script in `app.html`, toggled via `$lib/theme.ts`). The admin area always uses the light values via the `.admin-shell` wrapper in `admin/+layout.svelte`. Components read the variables directly — don't hardcode colors or add global `!important` overrides.

## Custom Markdown Syntax

Tags: `[name]`, `[handle]`, `[avatar]` (optional, filename in the `tweet-media` storage bucket), `[body]`, `[media]` (optional, comma-separated filenames — only the first `[media]` tag in a block is read), `[time]` (optional, defaults to "now" if omitted), `[likes]` (optional, `comments,retweets,likes`, defaults to `0,0,0`), `[replyingto]` (optional, "Replying to @x" context), `[unavailable]` (replaces every other tag in a block for a deleted/suspended tweet — normally inside `[quote]`).

URLs in body text are linked and shortened for display, and `#hashtags`/`@handles` are highlighted, at render time by `parseTwitterText()` — store plain text.

### Basic Tweet
```
[name]Steve Jobs[/name] [handle]@stevejobs[/handle] [body]Just released the iPhone. Revolutionary device that will change everything.[/body] [time]9:19 AM · Jan 9, 2007[/time] [likes]1240,892,5830[/likes]
```

### With Avatar and Media
```
[name]Steve Jobs[/name] [handle]@stevejobs[/handle] [avatar]stevejobs-avatar.jpg[/avatar] [body]Here's the new iPhone![/body] [media]iphone-reveal.jpg,keynote-video.mp4[/media] [time]9:19 AM · Jan 9, 2007[/time] [likes]1240,892,5830[/likes]
```

### Quote Tweet
```
[name]Steve Jobs[/name] [handle]@stevejobs[/handle] [body]Thoughts on this?[/body]
[quote]
  [name]Bill Gates[/name] [handle]@billgates[/handle] [body]The future of computing is mobile.[/body]
[/quote]
[time]9:19 AM · Jan 9, 2007[/time] [likes]240,92,830[/likes]
```

### Reply Chain
```
[name]Steve Jobs[/name] [handle]@stevejobs[/handle] [body]What do you think about the new iPhone?[/body] [time]9:19 AM · Jan 9, 2007[/time] [likes]1240,892,5830[/likes]
[reply]
  [name]Tim Cook[/name] [handle]@timcook[/handle] [time]9:25 AM · Jan 9, 2007[/time] [body]Incredible innovation! This will change everything.[/body] [likes]340,92,430[/likes]
[/reply]
```

A tweet block cannot have both `[quote]` and `[reply]` — the parser throws if both are present. Media/avatar filenames are resolved to public URLs via `supabase.storage.from('tweet-media').getPublicUrl(filename)`; there's no DB table tracking uploaded files, just the storage bucket plus the filename referenced in the markdown.

## Data Model

Parsed tweet shape is defined in `src/lib/utils/markdownParser.ts`; the database row type (`StoredTweet`) is in `src/lib/types/tweet.ts`.

```typescript
export interface TweetData {
  name: string;
  handle: string;
  body: string;
  avatar?: string;
  media?: string[];
  time?: string;
  likes?: string;        // "comments,retweets,likes" — use formatLikes() to get numbers
  quote?: TweetData;
  replies?: TweetData[];
  replyingTo?: string;   // "@handle"
  unavailable?: string;  // tombstone message for a deleted tweet
}

export interface ParseResult {
  success: boolean;
  data?: TweetData;
  error?: string;
}
```

## Database Schema

`.sql` at the repo root is now a verified reference of the live Supabase schema (checked directly via `information_schema`/`pg_policies`) — treat it as documentation, not something to run; the tables already exist and are populated. **This Supabase project is shared with several unrelated apps** (`bb_*`, `cl_*`, `pricedl_*`, `games`/`players`/`scores`, etc.) — only `tweets`, `current_featured_tweet`, and `featured_tweet_history` belong to this project.

What the app actually reads/writes:

```sql
CREATE TABLE tweets (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  title VARCHAR NOT NULL,               -- admin-only label, not shown publicly
  slug VARCHAR NOT NULL UNIQUE,         -- URL routing, generated from handle + random suffix
  markdown_content TEXT NOT NULL,       -- the bracket-tag markdown; parsed on read, not stored as JSON
  parsed_json JSONB,                    -- exists in the DB, unused by the app
  tweet_date TIMESTAMP,                 -- exists in the DB, unused by the app
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),
  updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);

-- "Tweet of the day" rotation, shown on the homepage
CREATE TABLE current_featured_tweet (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  tweet_id UUID REFERENCES tweets(id),
  featured_since DATE NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_DATE,
  updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
  -- single row; app deletes+reinserts to change it
);

CREATE TABLE featured_tweet_history (
  tweet_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES tweets(id),
  featured_date DATE NOT NULL,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),
  PRIMARY KEY (tweet_id, featured_date)
);
```

Storage: a public `tweet-media` bucket holds avatar/media files, referenced by filename from markdown tags. No `media_files`/`media` table exists (a `media_files` table does exist in this Supabase project, but it belongs to a different app and is unrelated to tweets).

**RLS is currently wide open**: `tweets`, `current_featured_tweet`, and `featured_tweet_history` each have an `ALL`/`USING (true)`/`WITH CHECK (true)` policy for the `public` role. The `@supabase/ssr` session gate in `admin/+layout.server.js` only protects rendering the `/admin/*` pages — it does not restrict database access. Since admin writes go through the plain anon-key client (`$lib/supabase.js`), anyone holding the anon key (shipped in the client bundle) can read, insert, update, or delete any tweet directly via the Supabase API, authenticated or not. Fixing this needs both a policy change (e.g. requiring `auth.role() = 'authenticated'` for writes) and switching admin mutations to a session-bound client that forwards the user's JWT — noted here, not applied, since it's a live database and the two changes need to land together.

Two minor, low-risk cleanup items confirmed live but not yet acted on: `tweets` has both `idx_tweets_slug` and the `UNIQUE` constraint's own index (`tweets_slug_key`) on the same `slug` column — one is redundant — and the `parsed_json`/`tweet_date` columns above are dead weight with no code path writing to them.

## Project Structure (actual)

```
src/
├── app.html                            # Inline script applies the saved public theme before first paint
├── app.css                             # Theme variables (dark/light/admin), Chirp font, base body styles
├── hooks.server.js                     # Supabase SSR client + safeGetSession per request
├── app.d.ts                            # Locals typing (supabase, safeGetSession)
├── lib/
│   ├── theme.ts                        # get/set public theme (data-theme on <html> + localStorage)
│   ├── actions/portal.ts               # Moves overlays (lightbox, toast) to <body>
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── UserTweetDisplay.svelte     # THE tweet renderer — public feed, tweet page, and every admin preview
│   │   ├── TweetMedia.svelte           # Twitter-style media grid (1 / 2 / 3 / 4 layouts, "+N" overflow)
│   │   ├── MediaLightbox.svelte        # Full-screen image viewer (arrows/Escape, portaled to <body>)
│   │   ├── TweetAvatar.svelte          # Avatar image with initials fallback when the file is missing
│   │   ├── FeaturedTweet.svelte        # Wraps UserTweetDisplay with the "Featured" label and glow
│   │   ├── FeedNavigation.svelte       # Theme toggle, sort toggle, debounced search for the home feed
│   │   ├── Navigation.svelte           # Admin top nav (rendered by admin/+layout.svelte)
│   │   └── TweetCreator.svelte         # /admin/create: markdown editor, uploads, samples, live preview
│   ├── utils/
│   │   ├── markdownParser.ts           # TweetMarkdownParser: parse/generate bracket-tag markdown; slug + likes helpers
│   │   ├── twitterClipboardParser.ts   # Parses copied X HTML or archiver-script JSON; media download via /admin/media-proxy
│   │   ├── twitterTextParser.js        # Body text → safe HTML (entity decoding, links, hashtag/handle highlight)
│   │   ├── media.ts                    # getMediaUrl(), isVideo()
│   │   ├── tweetAdmin.ts               # deleteTweet(), deleteMediaFiles(), referencedMediaFiles()
│   │   └── featuredTweet.js            # Featured-tweet rotation: get/set/rotate, 30-day no-repeat history
│   ├── types/tweet.ts                  # StoredTweet (a `tweets` row)
│   └── supabase.js                     # Anon-key Supabase client used by components/routes for data reads/writes
├── routes/
│   ├── +layout.svelte                  # Loads app.css
│   ├── +page.svelte                    # Home feed: search, sort (newest/oldest/shuffle), featured tweet, pagination
│   ├── +error.svelte
│   ├── [slug]/
│   │   ├── +page.server.js             # Loads one tweet by slug + its newer/older neighbours' slugs
│   │   └── +page.svelte                # Public single-tweet view (+ og/twitter link-preview tags)
│   └── admin/
│       ├── +layout.svelte              # .admin-shell light theme wrapper + Navigation
│       ├── +layout.server.js           # Redirects to /admin/login when there's no session (except the login page itself)
│       ├── +page.svelte                # Dashboard: counts, recent tweets, links
│       ├── login/, logout/             # Supabase email+password auth actions
│       ├── create/+page.svelte         # Uses TweetCreator
│       ├── parse/+page.svelte          # Import: paste copied X HTML or archiver JSON anywhere on the page
│       ├── featured/+page.svelte       # Manually set/rotate the featured tweet
│       ├── media-proxy/+server.js      # Admin-only fetch of X media (twimg hosts only) for the importer
│       ├── media-cleanup/+server.js    # Admin-only storage delete (abandoned uploads, deleted tweets)
│       ├── edit/[slug]/+page.server.js # Legacy URL — 308 redirect to /admin/tweets/[slug]/edit
│       └── tweets/
│           ├── +page.svelte            # List/search all tweets
│           └── [slug]/
│               ├── +page.svelte        # Single-tweet admin view, copy link/markdown, raw markdown
│               └── edit/+page.svelte   # Edit form + live preview + delete
tools/tampermonkey/museum-of-twitter-archiver.user.js   # Browser script: 📋 Archive button on x.com → clipboard JSON
```

## Key Behaviors Worth Knowing

- **One renderer**: `UserTweetDisplay.svelte` renders tweets everywhere (public and admin previews); the admin-only duplicate `TweetDisplay.svelte` was removed.
- **Slugs are permanent**: editing a tweet never changes its slug, since the slug is the public URL people share.
- **Deleting a tweet** (`deleteTweet()` in `tweetAdmin.ts`) removes its featured-tweet rows first (those foreign keys have no cascade), then the tweet, then every media file it references (main, quote, replies) via `/admin/media-cleanup`.
- **Uploads happen before saving** in `/admin/parse` and `/admin/create` so previews work; Clear (and re-pasting in `/admin/parse`) deletes uploads that never made it into a saved tweet. Closing the tab mid-draft still leaves them behind.
- **Featured tweet rotation** runs client-side on every homepage load (`loadFeaturedTweet()` in `+page.svelte`): checks whether today's rotation happened, fetches the current featured tweet, and initializes one if none exists. It is not cached or server-scheduled.
- **Feed preferences** (sort order, theme) persist in `localStorage`, not per-user in the DB.
- **Two tweet-import paths**: manual markdown entry (`TweetCreator.svelte`, used by `/admin/create`) and clipboard-HTML import (`twitterClipboardParser.ts`, used by `/admin/parse`). Both end up writing the same `{title, slug, markdown_content}` shape to `tweets`.
- **Engagement numbers**: the Tampermonkey script captures real counts; plain copy/paste doesn't carry them, so that path falls back to plausible synthetic numbers.
- **Admin writes use the plain anon-key client** (`$lib/supabase.js`), not a session-bound server client — write authorization is enforced by Supabase RLS policies, not by SvelteKit. The page-level session gate in `admin/+layout.server.js` only protects rendering the admin UI.

## Storage policies

`tweet-media` needs SELECT (public), INSERT (public, used by the anon client), and DELETE for `authenticated` only — deletes go through `/admin/media-cleanup`, which acts as the logged-in admin.

## Known Cleanup Candidates (not yet done — require a live-DB change, so flagged rather than applied)
- **RLS on `tweets`/`current_featured_tweet`/`featured_tweet_history` is fully open** to the `public` role (see Database Schema above) — the biggest one, since it means the admin login doesn't actually gate writes at the data layer.
- `tweets.parsed_json` and `tweets.tweet_date` columns (plus the GIN index on `parsed_json`) are live in the DB but unused by any code path.
- `tweets` has a redundant index: `idx_tweets_slug` duplicates the index the `UNIQUE (slug)` constraint already creates (`tweets_slug_key`).
- `current_featured_tweet.tweet_id` / `featured_tweet_history.tweet_id` foreign keys could be `ON DELETE CASCADE`; `deleteTweet()` works around it by deleting those rows first.

Already fixed: the old unused `types/tweet.ts` and `TweetParser.svelte` (plus the `@tiptap/*` deps) were deleted; `.sql` reflects the verified live schema; `TweetDisplay.svelte` was folded into `UserTweetDisplay.svelte`; the global `!important` theme overrides in `app.css` were removed.
